GlycanGT native inference kernel: R reimplementation adapted from
matsui-lab/GlycanGT commit 96611518c971deb89215ca163deaf9de3a59fa32.
https://github.com/matsui-lab/GlycanGT
The upstream code is distributed under Apache-2.0; the license is included in
licenses/GlycanGT-LICENSE. The R port changes the implementation language and
runs one canonical graph at a time with a recorded deterministic ORF seed policy.
The bundled monomer and linkage vocabulary tables derive from the same public
repository, preserving indices and appending the upstream [MASK] token.
The small test model is untrained and is not a distributed pretrained checkpoint.

GIFFLAR native network and molecular preprocessing: adapted from MIT-licensed
glycowork commit 199efdde6bc137dbbcd900f84f927fdbbca52eae.
https://github.com/BojarLab/glycowork
The MIT notice above applies. Residue templates are derived from the public
SKELETONS and _residue implementation in glycowork/motif/smiles.py. The R port
uses 27 explicitly supported residues with fixed-position modifications and
rejects other chemistry. Its network, graph construction and parser are
reimplemented in R. The shared vocabulary matches the pinned v12_lib.pkl
indices exactly. Pretrained weights are not distributed in this package.
